# November 20, 2026: St. Johnsville and its neighbours, Montgomery and Fulton counties, New York (region mohawk,
# drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny). The Atlas had nothing inside the village of St. Johnsville, nothing
# at Crum Creek or Mindenville, no entry for the village of Fort Plain as a whole, and only a dirt-road lead for the
# Yanney mill. Standing places mostly: the village and its Register buildings (Nellis Tavern, the stone grist mill,
# the Methodist church, the library, the Community House, the post office), the Crum Creek church, the
# Walrath-Van Horne house at Nelliston and the Fort Plain district; the canal ditches at Mindenville and the Yanney
# mill marker for traces.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); HMdb marker pages, the Pomeroy
# Foundation's marker pages, palatinesettlementsociety.org, mohawkvalleymuseums.us, sjvny.org (the village),
# visitmontgomerycountyny.com (county tourism), theoldhouselife.com (a 2023 sale listing) and crumcreekchurchny
# .blogspot.com through tools/page.py. National Register forms for these listings are NPGallery placeholders and were
# not read.
