  'The Palatine Settlement Society has restored it to about 1835, its tavern years, with an herb garden on the grounds and a yearly Rhubarb Festival (Wikipedia, mohawkvalleymuseums.us). Wikipedia\'s photographs show a yellow clapboard house on a stone basement with brick chimneys, and a furnished tavern room on the first floor; which fabric is original not checked.',
  'An 18th-century Palatine farmhouse kept as the turnpike tavern it became.',
