  'The three-storey limestone mill and its house. The county tourism listing says the mill has three secret rooms under the basement used to hide people escaping slavery, and a 1,000-foot tunnel for the waterwheel; that is a local story, not checked against any other source. Interior not open to the public as far as any source read says.',
